1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:24,400
Remember, none of that sneaky crap. Got it?

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:40,000
About time. Though you didn't make it easy.

3
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Yeah, that was real rude. I found them nearby like you said. Oh yeah, I figured you'd want me to bring her too.

4
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:03,000
Face it, you lost and now you're all out of tricks.

5
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:09,000
No. Why are you here?

6
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Well, isn't this sweet? A nice family reunion. Now get over here.

7
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:30,000
I see. If that's your choice, then so be it.

8
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,000
No!

9
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:46,000
I have something I want to ask first. The photo. Who gave it to Lu Guang that night? Was it you?

10
00:01:46,000 --> 00:02:08,000
What photo are you talking about? The kid was at the hospital, but he was helping me. You wrote the hand off, right?

11
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:15,000
It's just you. So what's up? Are you my new babysitter?

12
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Ha! Well, then I'm telling you right now. I don't need you here.

13
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:27,000
Okay, what's that supposed to mean?

14
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Oh, I see. Damn, that is good. Really thinking ahead.

15
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:37,000
Ha! You take care of that now.

16
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:41,000
Creepy little ninja almost got his nose.

17
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:48,000
Really? I thought you were looking for your sister.

18
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Why would I lie to you?

19
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:56,000
I don't know. Why would you?

20
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:06,000
It was you. Your sister told us.

21
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:11,000
I thought it... might change the past.

22
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:18,000
The truth comes out. Must everyone betray me? Hand over the phone.

23
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:23,000
Hang on, boss. Why are you acting all surprised about this?

24
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:29,000
You knew. I told you. That night at the station. Why are you calling him out now?

25
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:33,000
He should have handed it over. Not doing it just proves he's got a motive.

26
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:38,000
What? Oh! You already figured that out, didn't you?

27
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:56,000
Idiot. Such a waste. Though I did like your obedience.

28
00:03:56,000 --> 00:04:01,000
Sadly, you never knew when to shut up.

29
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:04,000
And now everyone knows too much.

30
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:10,000
You knew this whole time.

31
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:13,000
You played ignorant so you could keep using me.

32
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:16,000
He never trusted you to start with.

33
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:22,000
Shut up! I was clear! I cannot abide betrayal! I won't! Ever!

34
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:24,000
And yet you still did it!

35
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:28,000
From the beginning, all we've ever done was use each other.

36
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:31,000
You can't betray that.

37
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:33,000
How can you say that to me?

38
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:37,000
I took care of you, raised you and your mute sister like you were my own!

39
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:43,000
That's crap! You didn't raise them like family. Just your tools!

40
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:49,000
You don't get to judge me! You don't know anything about my life!

41
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:59,000
But then, none of it matters anyway. Not really.

42
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:08,000
You can go back. Fix it all. Take it. Make a world where none of this had to happen.

43
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:35,000
This is all because of her. She's the mistake that needs to be fixed! Now do it!

44
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:36,000
Now do it!

45
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:44,000
What happened here? Did a gas pipe explode?

46
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:46,000
I don't know. Someone called the fire department.

47
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:48,000
I'm on the phone with them now.

48
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:51,000
You don't need to get back up.

49
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:52,000
You're gonna need backup...

50
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:56,000
You're gonna need backup!

51
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:59,000
You're gonna need backup...

52
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:02,000
You're gonna need backup!

53
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:04,000
I'm gonna need backup!

54
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:07,000
I need backup!

55
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:12,000
I took my phone!

56
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:15,000
Police. Everyone get back and stay out of the way!

57
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:15,960
Get out of here, Bass.

58
00:06:22,460 --> 00:06:23,880
Thank goodness you're right.

59
00:06:25,880 --> 00:06:27,520
Hey, you okay?

60
00:06:28,060 --> 00:06:28,720
Where are the others?

61
00:06:30,660 --> 00:06:32,120
It happened so fast.

62
00:06:32,360 --> 00:06:33,600
I thought we were almost free.

63
00:06:34,320 --> 00:06:35,960
And everything collapsed around us.

64
00:06:36,260 --> 00:06:37,600
We were knocked out for a moment.

65
00:06:38,320 --> 00:06:40,420
Once we came to, we started helping who we could.

66
00:06:40,420 --> 00:06:40,940
Shang-Chi-Shan?

67
00:06:41,580 --> 00:06:42,380
Where is he?

68
00:06:42,380 --> 00:06:46,280
Are people still in the theater?

69
00:06:46,340 --> 00:06:47,340
They need to get in there.

70
00:06:50,040 --> 00:06:51,240
Someone knocked me out.

71
00:06:51,900 --> 00:06:53,260
They took him and Li Tianxi.

72
00:06:53,880 --> 00:06:54,800
I don't know where,

73
00:06:55,720 --> 00:06:56,940
but they couldn't have gotten far.

74
00:06:57,760 --> 00:06:58,560
Not with all this.

75
00:06:59,040 --> 00:07:00,940
Police would be all over the area soon.

76
00:07:01,940 --> 00:07:03,120
They'll put this place on lockdown.

77
00:07:03,940 --> 00:07:05,800
No one's getting in or out without being checked.

78
00:07:07,060 --> 00:07:07,580
Right.

79
00:07:07,580 --> 00:07:10,600
Then why would they set off the explosion in the first place?

80
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:14,380
Unless, we already had some other way to escape.

81
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:16,840
They had me somewhere underground.

82
00:07:17,360 --> 00:07:18,700
I know because I heard the subway.

83
00:07:19,880 --> 00:07:22,760
If they had access, they could run.

84
00:07:23,960 --> 00:07:24,520
Possibly.

85
00:07:24,520 --> 00:07:28,480
It's midnight.

86
00:07:29,200 --> 00:07:30,560
So the subways won't be running.

87
00:07:31,360 --> 00:07:32,140
Or which line?

88
00:07:32,500 --> 00:07:32,860
Cao Hua.

89
00:07:36,940 --> 00:07:37,900
In the warehouse,

90
00:07:38,400 --> 00:07:40,580
there were boxes from a bakery at Cao Hua Station.

91
00:07:43,380 --> 00:07:44,260
That's close.

92
00:07:44,620 --> 00:07:46,640
But that line runs north and south.

93
00:07:46,740 --> 00:07:47,620
Then we'll split up.

94
00:07:47,620 --> 00:07:51,140
Fine.

95
00:07:51,840 --> 00:07:52,560
Stay safe.

96
00:07:53,180 --> 00:07:54,100
And stay smart.

97
00:07:54,100 --> 00:08:01,260
I'm not asking for much here.

98
00:08:02,200 --> 00:08:04,980
Just go back and stop her from meeting Zhuang Shuai.

99
00:08:07,140 --> 00:08:09,800
Why is that more important than stopping her murder?

100
00:08:10,300 --> 00:08:11,640
He thought she betrayed him.

101
00:08:12,980 --> 00:08:14,220
So he killed her.

102
00:08:15,560 --> 00:08:16,080
Bullshit!

103
00:08:16,080 --> 00:08:19,000
I saw what they were doing behind my back.

104
00:08:19,340 --> 00:08:20,680
They barely hid it!

105
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:23,980
You also asked me to kill him.

106
00:08:25,220 --> 00:08:26,600
Or did you forget?

107
00:08:28,120 --> 00:08:30,020
When my sister and I worked together,

108
00:08:30,240 --> 00:08:32,580
I can do a lot more than just control someone.

109
00:08:34,480 --> 00:08:36,340
I can look into their memories.

110
00:08:36,340 --> 00:08:50,300
You were so convinced of their betrayal

111
00:08:50,300 --> 00:08:52,120
that you never asked me what I saw.

112
00:08:52,880 --> 00:08:54,200
I saw them rehearse,

113
00:08:54,800 --> 00:08:55,140
eat,

114
00:08:56,260 --> 00:08:56,880
talk,

115
00:08:57,600 --> 00:08:58,700
and perform.

116
00:08:59,600 --> 00:09:00,820
That was all.

117
00:09:02,960 --> 00:09:04,760
No one's coming to see the play.

118
00:09:04,760 --> 00:09:06,100
I'm worried.

119
00:09:06,520 --> 00:09:08,080
The theater might close down.

120
00:09:09,180 --> 00:09:10,120
It sucks.

121
00:09:10,460 --> 00:09:12,280
But there's not much we can do about it.

122
00:09:12,580 --> 00:09:13,400
Theater's costly.

123
00:09:14,060 --> 00:09:15,660
Not everyone can afford it.

124
00:09:16,300 --> 00:09:18,000
We barely charge for tickets, though.

125
00:09:18,280 --> 00:09:19,740
Maybe it's the subway noise?

126
00:09:20,760 --> 00:09:21,280
Oh, hey.

127
00:09:21,720 --> 00:09:22,560
Are you free tonight?

128
00:09:23,300 --> 00:09:24,440
I found a new venue.

129
00:09:24,980 --> 00:09:26,180
And it might be cheaper.

130
00:09:27,460 --> 00:09:28,400
Unfortunately, no.

131
00:09:28,800 --> 00:09:30,000
But why show it at night?

132
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:31,220
That's kind of weird.

133
00:09:31,820 --> 00:09:32,440
You can go.

134
00:09:33,100 --> 00:09:34,880
It's not like we're the boss or anything.

135
00:09:36,080 --> 00:09:37,780
It's an office space right now.

136
00:09:38,160 --> 00:09:40,020
They haven't officially put it on the market.

137
00:09:40,640 --> 00:09:42,720
We'd have to wait for the tenants to clear out.

138
00:09:43,420 --> 00:09:45,460
My husband hates it when I come home late.

139
00:09:46,160 --> 00:09:47,500
A perk of his job.

140
00:09:47,780 --> 00:09:48,580
Always worried.

141
00:09:48,580 --> 00:09:51,300
Or he just loves you.

142
00:09:51,300 --> 00:09:58,220
Well, you can see the design of this place doesn't work as an office.

143
00:09:58,940 --> 00:10:00,560
But for a theater, it's great.

144
00:10:00,820 --> 00:10:02,180
You could make it so unique.

145
00:10:02,860 --> 00:10:03,700
Excuse me.

146
00:10:03,980 --> 00:10:04,840
I'll be one second.

147
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:07,960
Hey.

148
00:10:08,420 --> 00:10:08,960
What's up?

149
00:10:09,560 --> 00:10:10,220
You're at home?

150
00:10:10,900 --> 00:10:12,340
I thought you were still at work.

151
00:10:13,140 --> 00:10:13,400
No.

152
00:10:13,780 --> 00:10:14,860
We closed the case.

153
00:10:15,500 --> 00:10:16,840
And why are you still out?

154
00:10:16,840 --> 00:10:19,520
Oh, I'm checking out a new venue.

155
00:10:20,180 --> 00:10:20,820
This late?

156
00:10:21,360 --> 00:10:22,220
All by yourself?

157
00:10:24,460 --> 00:10:25,500
I'm not alone.

158
00:10:25,980 --> 00:10:26,820
Da Shui is here.

159
00:10:27,080 --> 00:10:27,600
It's fine.

160
00:10:28,520 --> 00:10:29,540
Who is that?

161
00:10:30,440 --> 00:10:30,960
Right.

162
00:10:31,460 --> 00:10:33,000
We were in my last play together.

163
00:10:33,780 --> 00:10:34,500
You'll meet him.

164
00:10:34,780 --> 00:10:36,360
But for right now, we're busy.

165
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:37,320
See you soon.

166
00:10:40,060 --> 00:10:40,900
Sorry for that.

167
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:41,680
Let's continue.

168
00:10:41,680 --> 00:10:53,000
Every day they were on that stage.

169
00:10:53,580 --> 00:10:55,220
Being so intimate.

170
00:10:55,880 --> 00:10:57,680
All those rehearsals and late night dinners.

171
00:10:58,440 --> 00:10:59,940
They were always together.

172
00:11:02,160 --> 00:11:03,780
How could it be innocent?

173
00:11:04,400 --> 00:11:05,980
How is she not betraying me?

174
00:11:06,740 --> 00:11:07,600
She lied.

175
00:11:07,940 --> 00:11:09,340
I never make mistakes.

176
00:11:09,680 --> 00:11:11,540
There's no way I was wrong.

177
00:11:11,680 --> 00:11:14,800
They know what they did to me.

178
00:11:15,640 --> 00:11:17,260
They got what they deserved.

179
00:11:18,100 --> 00:11:19,300
You are insane.

180
00:11:19,540 --> 00:11:20,840
What are you talking about?

181
00:11:22,700 --> 00:11:24,560
I can still fit into it.

182
00:11:25,520 --> 00:11:27,460
Sure, I gained a few pounds after the wedding.

183
00:11:27,860 --> 00:11:29,460
But a little dieting will fix that.

184
00:11:35,160 --> 00:11:36,780
